page DatabaseEntitiesPage
  Section id:"database-entities-introduction" py:{ xs:6 md:10 }
    Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:"1fr auto" } gap:5 align:"end"
      Grid columns:1 gap:3
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "SERVER / DATABASE / ENTITIES"
        Title size:{ xs:"3xl" md:"6xl" } weight:"black"
          "Entities"
        Text size:"lg" color:"muted"
          "An entity is an importable server contract that names a table, its fields, and the constraints Dowe can lower into deterministic PostgreSQL or D1 migrations. Dowe Database remains schema-less and does not create a local SQL schema from entities."
      Button href:"/docs/server/db" variant:"ghost" scheme:"muted" size:"sm"
        "Database overview"
  Section id:"database-entities-declaration" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "DECLARATION"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Describe one table with explicit fields"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "The declaration name is a server binding. Dowe converts it to a lower-snake-case table name, so SmsDeliveries targets sms_deliveries. Every entity must declare at least one field and may declare at most one primary field."
      Code:
        language:"dowe"
        variant:"soft"
        scheme:"surface"
        copyLabel:"Copy entity"
        copiedLabel:"Copied"
        content:"""
          entity SmsDeliveries
            id:string primary:true
            recipient:string required:true index:true
            providerMessageId:string unique:true
            status:string required:true index:true
            attempts:int required:true
            cost:decimal
            createdAt:timestamp required:true index:true
            metadata:json
        """
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:3 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "Binding"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "SmsDeliveries is the symbol imported by Database config and referenced by a seeder."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "Table"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "The compiler derives sms_deliveries from the entity name. Query operations still use the table string."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "Implicit primary"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "When no field is marked primary and an id field exists, Dowe promotes that id field to required primary. It does not add a missing id field to an entity."
  Section id:"database-entities-types" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "FIELD TYPES"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Use the implemented portable type set"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Entity field types are fixed and validated during compilation. The provider migration maps each type to its current SQL representation."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 lg:3 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "string"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "TEXT on PostgreSQL and D1."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "bool"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "BOOLEAN on PostgreSQL and INTEGER on D1."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "int"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "BIGINT on PostgreSQL and INTEGER on D1."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "number"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "DOUBLE PRECISION on PostgreSQL and REAL on D1."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "decimal"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "DOUBLE PRECISION on PostgreSQL and NUMERIC on D1 in the current generator."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "timestamp"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "TEXT on both providers."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "json"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "JSONB on PostgreSQL and TEXT on D1."
  Section id:"database-entities-constraints" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "CONSTRAINTS"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Make storage requirements visible"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Constraint props are boolean and belong after the field type. Unknown props, duplicate fields, unsupported types, and multiple primary fields fail compilation."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"primary" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "primary"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "Creates the single PRIMARY KEY and also makes the field NOT NULL."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "required"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "Emits NOT NULL for PostgreSQL and D1 migrations."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "unique"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "Emits a UNIQUE constraint for the field."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "index"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "Emits a deterministic secondary index named from the table and field."
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "Entities do not currently declare foreign keys, relations, defaults, compound indexes, or provider-specific column types."
  Section id:"database-entities-modules" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "MODULES AND DATABASE CONFIG"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Import the entity into one server-only handle"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Keep entity declarations under server/entities and import them into a shared Database config module. The entities list selects the migration contracts owned by that handle."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 lg:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"primary" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:3
            Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" color:"primary"
              "server/entities/sms-delivery-entity.dowe"
            Code:
              language:"dowe"
              variant:"soft"
              scheme:"surface"
              copyLabel:"Copy entity module"
              copiedLabel:"Copied"
              content:"""
                entity SmsDeliveries
                  id:string primary:true
                  recipient:string required:true index:true
                  status:string required:true index:true
                  createdAt:timestamp required:true
              """
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:3
            Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" color:"muted"
              "server/config/database.dowe"
            Code:
              language:"dowe"
              variant:"soft"
              scheme:"surface"
              copyLabel:"Copy Database config"
              copiedLabel:"Copied"
              content:"""
                import SmsDeliveries from "@/server/entities/sms-delivery-entity"

                database appDb provider:"postgres"
                  host:env.POSTGRES_HOST
                  port:env.POSTGRES_PORT
                  account:env.POSTGRES_USER
                  secret:env.POSTGRES_PASSWORD
                  name:env.POSTGRES_DATABASE
                  entities:[SmsDeliveries]
                  seeders:[]
              """
  Section id:"database-entities-provider-behavior" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "PROVIDER BEHAVIOR"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Know what the entity controls"
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:3 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "PostgreSQL"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "Dowe generates deterministic CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX migration SQL and applies pending migrations before the production listener opens."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "Cloudflare D1"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "Dowe generates the equivalent SQLite-compatible migration artifacts and applies them before seeders."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Grid columns:1 gap:2
            Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
              "Dowe Database"
            Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
              "The local and remote Dowe engines stay dynamic. Entity metadata does not create a schema or reject undeclared record fields at runtime."
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "A query still uses db:<handle>.<operation> and a table string. An entity is compile-time schema and migration authority for SQL providers, not a runtime Database handle and not a value exposed to Views."
